{
  "configuration_id": "config_026",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_024 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) achieved the best performance so far (acc 0.629, F1 0.599), a large jump over the singleprofile multimodal baseline (0.535). This shows multiprofile aggregation is a critical design axis. However, we only have one multiprofile data point and do not yet know whether avgpool is near-optimal or whether a more expressive aggregation (transformer) can further exploit the multi-view structure. config_026 tests transformer aggregation while holding all other parameters at their best-known values (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, concat fusion). This is the best next experiment because it directly exploits the strongest evidence (the multiprofile+multimodal direction) while resolving key uncertainty about the aggregation mechanism—information that will guide all subsequent multiprofile experiments across encoders and fusion strategies. It is more informative than testing weighted fusion (config_025) because the singleprofile data already suggests concat≈weighted, whereas the aggregation choice is an unexplored axis with potentially larger impact."
}

